  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1131 PM CDT TUE OCT 27 2026\n\nOver the next few days, upper-level ridging will continue to\nbreak down as a broad trough begins to establish itself out west.\nDue to this broad troughing pattern, flow aloft will transition\nback to the SW, allowing for moisture to return to the airmass\noverhead. As we get closer to the weekend, a weak system will\nbegin to work into the central Plains, with a series of leading\nimpulses branching off to the south. It's these disturbances that\nwill allow for rain to return to the forecast through the\nweekend, with the bulk of the rain falling on Saturday, and low\nrain probabilities lingering through Sunday.\n\nThe new workweek should start on the dry side, with no additional\nrainfall expected through Tuesday. With that being said, long-\nrange guidance has been consistently highlighting a broader\npattern breakdown towards the middle of the week. While the exact\nimpacts from this pattern breakdown remain to be seen, current\nguidance suggests additional rain activity, and a swing back to\nmuch colder temperatures.\n\n/44/",
